.TH expr_format 3 2026-10-23 "Graph Drawer expr man-pages 1.0.13"
.SH NAME
expr_vwritef[t][_r], expr_writef[t][_r], expr_[v]apwritef[t][_r], expr_[v]sprintf[t][_r] \- string formatter
.SH LIBRARY
Graph Drawer Expression Evaluator Library
.RI ( libexpr ,\~ \-lexpr )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.BR #include\~"expr.h"
.P
.BI "ssize_t expr_vwritef[t][_r](expr_writer " writer ",intptr_t " fd ",const char *restrict " fmt ",size_t " fmtlen ",expr_argfetch " arg ",intptr_t " addr ",[const struct expr_ftable *restrict " table "],[const struct expr_memtool *restrict " mtl "]);"
.BI "ssize_t expr_writef[t][_r](expr_writer " writer ",intptr_t " fd ",const char *restrict " fmt ",size_t " fmtlen ",const union expr_argf *restrict " args ",size_t " arglen ",[const struct expr_ftable *restrict " table "],[const struct expr_memtool *restrict " mtl "]);"
.BI "ssize_t expr_vapwritef[t][_r](expr_writer " writer ",intptr_t " fd ",const char *restrict " fmt ",size_t " fmtlen ",[const struct expr_ftable *restrict " table "],[const struct expr_memtool *restrict " mtl "],va_list " ap ");"
.BI "ssize_t expr_apwritef[t][_r](expr_writer " writer ",intptr_t " fd ",const char *restrict " fmt ",size_t " fmtlen ",[const struct expr_ftable *restrict " table "],[const struct expr_memtool *restrict " mtl "]," ... ");"
.BI "ssize_t expr_vsnprintf[t][_r](char *" buf ",size_t " buflen ",const char *restrict " fmt ",size_t " fmtlen ",[const struct expr_ftable *restrict " table "],[const struct expr_memtool *restrict " mtl "],va_list " ap ");"
.BI "ssize_t expr_snprintf[t][_r](char *" buf ",size_t " buflen ",const char *restrict " fmt ",size_t " fmtlen ",[const struct expr_ftable *restrict " table "],[const struct expr_memtool *restrict " mtl "]," ... ");"
.BI "ssize_t expr_vasprintf[t][_r](char **" strp ",const char *restrict " fmt ",size_t " fmtlen ",[const struct expr_ftable *restrict " table "],[const struct expr_memtool *restrict " mtl "],va_list " ap ");"
.BI "ssize_t expr_asprintf[t][_r](char **" strp ",const char *restrict " fmt ",size_t " fmtlen ",[const struct expr_ftable *restrict " table "],[const struct expr_memtool *restrict " mtl "]," ... ");"
.BI "extern const struct expr_ftable " expr_ftable_default "[1];"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR expr_vwritef[t][_r]()
function write the string formatted under
.IR fmt [ fmtlen ]
to
.I fd
by
.IR writer .
The arguments are fetched from
.I addr
by
.IR arg.
.P
The
.BR expr_writef[t][_r]()
function fetch the argument from
.IR args [ arglen ].
.P
The
.BR expr_[v]apwritef[t][_r]()
function fetch the argument from
.IR "... " or " ap" .
.P
The
.BR expr_[v]snprintf[t][_r]()
function write the formatted string to
.IR buf [ buflen ].
.P
The
.BR expr_[v]asprintf[t][_r]()
macro write the formatted string to a space with enough size and let
.IR *strp
point to it. The space must be deallocated by
.I mtl
->
.B deallocate()
when it is no longer needed.
.SS DEFAULT FORMAT
Defined by
.IR expr_ftable_default .
.P
"%[flags][width][.digit][:argsize]conversion_character"
.P
width, digit, argsize can be "*", to read from argumant, or be "**" to read from the pointer provided by argument.
.TP
.B %
% .
.TQ
.B s
Standard string.
.TQ
.B S
String with length
.IR digit .
.TQ
.B f
double.
.TQ
.B d
.RB "signed integer(" ssize_t ")."
.TQ
.B u 
.RB "unsigned integer(" size_t ")."
.TQ
.B x
.RB "unsigned integer(" size_t "), in hex."
.TQ
.B o
.RB "unsigned integer(" size_t "), in octal."
.TQ
.B b
.RB "unsigned integer(" size_t "), in binary."
.TQ 
.BR m , M
.RB "unsigned integer(" size_t "), in human readable format."
.TQ
.B c
Character.
.TQ
.BR h , H
Hexdump from the pointer provided by argument the with length
.IR digit .
.TQ
.B p , P
Address of a pointer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR expr_[v||vap|ap]writef[t][_r]()
return the number of bytes written. On error or truncate, the negative code or the truncated size added by
.B SSIZE_MIN+128
will return.
.P
The
.BR expr_[v]snprintf[t][_r]()
return the number of bytes should be written to
.IR buf " (excluding the terminating zero)"
in the case that the space is enough. The return value that >=
.I buflen
means the output was truncated.
.P
The
.BR expr_[v]asprintf[t][_r]()
return the number of bytes be written to
.IR *strp " (excluding the terminating zero)"
on success, or negative value on
.RI "fail(and " *strp " will be undefined)."
.SH ATTRIBUTES
.TS
allbox;
lbx lb lb
l l l.
Interface	Attribute	Value
T{
.na
